        <h3>Answer 1</h3>
        <div class="question-box">What is the difference between a class and an object?</div>
        <div class="fragment box-blue">
            <p>A class is a blueprint; an object is an instance with its own state and behaviour.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h3>Answer 2</h3>
        <div class="question-box">Why do we use encapsulation?</div>
        <div class="fragment box-blue">
            <p>To protect internal state, enforce invariants, and expose a controlled interface.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h3>Answer 3</h3>
        <div class="question-box">How many copies of a static variable exist?</div>
        <div class="fragment box-blue">
            <p>One shared copy at the class level.</p>
        </div>
    </section>
